Compressed (UBWC) render targets: cleared, drawn into, sampled, fetched and copied out compressed (2026-11-12,
darwin-lisa session 9). The plug-in asks for them with boot-arg metal_ubwc_rt=1 (HakiosMetalCA-ubwc-rt.patch).

The core already laid out a compressed RGBA8/BGRA8 texture (fdl6_layout with UBWC) for the textures the GPU only
samples, filled from staged rows by the 2D engine, and mrtWords already gave a compressed target its flag buffer and
RB_RENDER_CNTL.FLAG_MRTS. What a render target needs beyond that, here:

1. Texture::make: a compressed render target may also be RGBA16Float (CoreAnimation's backdrop format; UBWC takes
   FMT6_16_16_16_16_FLOAT, fd6_resource.cc ok_ubwc_format). Never a texture a kernel writes, never more than one level.
2. mrtWords: a compressed target is named WZYX whatever the format's swap, as turnip names it (fd6_pipe2swap: "the
   CCU ignores swap and always uses WZYX when tiled"); the TP reads the layout WZYX too (the descriptor), so the
   registers say what the hardware does.
3. levelDescriptor (a framebuffer fetch's view of an attachment) carries the UBWC words too (Texture::applyUbwc,
   shared with sampledDescriptor); a swizzled view keeps them; a view of a compressed render target is the texture
   itself or refused (another format would read the tiles as something they are not).
4. A Clear of a compressed target: the 2D engine's solid fill into the UBWC view (TILE6_3, WZYX, FLAGS and the flag
   buffer, as r2d_dst over a UBWC view does), which writes a few bytes a block. checkTarget refused it before.
5. A copy out of a compressed texture (blit, texture to buffer): the 2D engine reads it compressed (SP_PS_2D_SRC_INFO
   TILE6_3 | FLAGS, WZYX, SP_PS_2D_SRC_FLAGS), into a linear or a compressed destination. encodeBlit refused it before.
6. The fake GPU takes a UBWC target (TILE6_3, WZYX, its FLAG_MRTS bit, a flag buffer in reach), a fill into a UBWC
   image and a copy out of one written before, counting them (ubwcDraws, ubwcFills, ubwcReads), and keeps refusing a
   tiled target without its flags.

The CPU still never reads or writes a compressed render target (replace and read refuse it): the plug-in compresses
only private and memoryless storage, which Metal does not let the CPU touch.

Host: 266 tests (two new: a_compressed_render_target_is_cleared_drawn_sampled_and_copied_out_compressed, BGRA8 and
RGBA16Float; a_compressed_texture_is_refused_where_its_layout_is_not_served), the same 4 tests / 14 checks failing as
before the patch (pre-existing: the unbound-buffer refusals the earlier patches lifted). Not run on the phone yet.

